# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
service-account.json

# Meeting findings, anything derived from them, and the drafted write-ups are
# published through the review branch, never committed straight to main. Twice
# in one session a stray `git add -A` swept them onto main, once while the
# commit message claimed the opposite. The workflow that is meant to publish
# them passes `-f` deliberately; nothing else picks them up by accident.
data/lake-watch/meetings/*.json
data/lake-watch/commitments.json
content/news/*-council-meeting.md
